{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790726512,"nonce":"loh8BQ/CshQ+SN+aDSlHq5YyEao=","title":"Tiered host dispatch locks the profiling map on every call","message":"TieredBackend::record_call reads ProfileData function_counts and then record_function_call takes the map write lock. This is paid by every host invocation after native promotion even though the function and its counter are already registered and stable.\n\nThe production sample_rate path also uses the sampled count as its clock: after the first increment to 1, a rate of 10 skips forever because that count no longer advances. A rate of zero reaches modulo zero despite its comment.\n\nCache the profile counter in FunctionEntry, keep a separate atomic call clock for sampling, and preserve counter identities when statistics are reset. Host dispatch can then record samples without a map lock.","files":null}]}